"""Memory notes (2026-10-05, P-M1): the store, the block, the router's reads and the routes, on any
machine (no torch). The prompt-level tests (positions, replay, identity with memory off) are in
tests/test_memory_router.py, which needs torch.

The test matrix:

  1  the file format round-trips (frontmatter, body, changelog); a file without an id is skipped
                                                        test_note_format
  2  add: a provisional file under its scope, 0600, the user's INDEX.md regenerated by the
     nightly job; project and session notes need their project and session
                                                        test_add_and_scopes
  3  dedupe: the same title (any case, punctuation) or a near copy in the same scope becomes a
     revision (old body under revisions/, a changelog line); another scope is a new note
                                                        test_dedupe_to_revision
  4  caps are refusals: title, body, session notes; never clipped
                                                        test_caps
  5  secrets: redacted on disk and counted; a body that is mostly a secret is refused
                                                        test_secrets
  6  a rule about the user from a tool turn is refused; update/archive of an unknown or foreign
     id is refused; a model revision of a ratified note sends it back to provisional; pinning
     needs a ratified rule                              test_rules_in_code
  7  search: the request's own scopes only, session over project over user at equal score,
     archived and stale notes left out                  test_search
  8  archive, delete, nightly (old archives deleted, duplicates counted), export, user delete
                                                        test_archive_nightly_export
     the model's archive of a ratified note keeps it, provisional again with the reason in its
     changelog; its own provisional notes it archives; Memory.take writes no state line for
     it                                   test_model_archive_of_a_ratified_note
  9  the block parser: attributes and head lines, defaults, schema errors
                                                        test_block_parse
 10  the stream filter: a block split over many pieces is held back, the text around it goes
     out; a fifth block, a refused block and one over 2,000 characters are hidden too (SRV-277);
     an unclosed block and one still open past the hold limit go out as text; `<tandem_memoryx`
     is not ours                                        test_stream_filter
 11  token spans: a block on whole tokens is found; one whose edge shares a token with text is
     not                                                test_token_spans
 12  the router: memory off adds nothing; shadow adds the card only; on adds the card, the index
     once and the bodies on a new message (never on a tool turn), no user: nothing
                                                        test_router_attach
 13  Memory.take: a written block, a refused one, the state line, the journal row without text
                                                        test_take
 14  the model's routes need the session address; search, read, write
                                                        test_model_routes
 15  the dashboard's routes: list, one, edit (ratified, human), pin, archive, delete, search,
     export, user delete with confirmation              test_admin_routes
 17  SRV-277: an Open WebUI chat (no working directory) writes a project-scoped block: the note
     lands at user scope (rescoped, journaled), no markup reaches the answer; a block the store
     refuses (schema, a rule from a tool turn) is hidden with its reason journaled; the hidden
     blocks' tokens are found as spans for the next turn's end alignment
                                                        test_srv277_owui_block_never_shown
 16  P-M3: a `propose` block becomes a proposal (never applied), Apply is a new packages version
     with the text and the old version restores it, a replacement of a changed text is refused,
     an append applies to the text as it is, Reject keeps the reason; no evidence without J1 rows
                                                        test_proposals

All text is synthetic. Run: python tests/test_memory_notes.py
"""

